schema: resource
object:
  title: Murmurations Protocol
  type: resource
  resource_type: standard
  url: https://docs.murmurations.network/guides/create-a-schema.html
  is_source_system_candidate: true
  toolkit_route: Layer 2 (Knowledge Commons) / metadata standards, federation
  link_status: active
  related_concepts:
    - Type vs. Tag (metadata discipline)
  related_resources:
    - Dublin Core
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/metadata-that-matters.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  notes: >-
    A regen-adjacent network protocol maintaining a public field library of
    pre-defined, reusable metadata fields (e.g. `longitude`, not `long`).
    Cited as the example of why shared field names matter across a network
    of communities — directly analogous to this toolkit's own federation
    concerns. Flagged is_source_system_candidate: true — a future ingest
    pass could register Murmurations as a full source-system peer (it
    maintains a living, updatable field library, not a static document).
